# Normalise line endings on the way into git, and check every text file out
# with LF regardless of platform.
#
# Without this a Windows clone gets CRLF from core.autocrlf, and any tool that
# reads the file expecting LF disagrees with the working copy while CI, which
# runs on Linux, never sees it. That is the worst shape of disagreement: green
# in CI and red locally, so a developer trying to reproduce a passing build
# cannot.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must not be touched by the rules above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
